            <ArticleTitle>Systemic vasculitis presenting with massive bowel infarction.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>692-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Gastrointestinal involvement in systemic vasculitis occurs in up to 30% of patients. Fortunately intestinal infarction is a rare complication, but if present carries a high mortality, and swift management of the underlying vasculitis is crucial. Two such cases are described.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
